#: src/borrowing/exercise.md:128
msgid ""
"The goal of this exercise is to practice the core concepts of ownership and "
"borrowing, specifically the rule that you cannot mutate a collection while "
"holding a reference to one of its elements."
msgstr ""

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md:131
msgid ""
"`add_spell` should take ownership of a `Spell` and move it into the "
"`Wizard`'s inventory."
msgstr ""

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md:133
msgid "`cast_spell` is the core of the exercise. It needs to:"
msgstr ""

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md:134
msgid "Find the spell (by index or by reference)."
msgstr ""

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md:135
msgid "Check mana and decrement it."
msgstr ""

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md:136
msgid "Decrement the spell's `uses`."
msgstr ""

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md:137
msgid "Remove the spell if `uses == 0`."
msgstr ""

#: src/borrowing/exercise.md:138
msgid ""
"**Borrow Checker Conflict:** If students try to hold a reference to the "
"spell (e.g., `let spell = &mut self.spells[i]`) and then call `self.spells."
"remove(i)` while that reference is still \"alive\" in the same scope, the "
"borrow checker will complain. This is a great opportunity to show how to "
"structure code to satisfy the borrow checker (e.g., by using indices or by "
"ensuring the borrow ends before the mutation)."
msgstr ""
